      "writtenOn": "2022-11-21T18:29:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Right now transferToRecording is just about handling ref tracking, but I think we can encapsulate staging buffer management completely into DrawBufferManager if we have transferToRecording() be responsible for creating the buffer-to-buffer copy tasks that move data from staging to private buffer.\n\nThe `fUsedBuffers` list can be updated to hold the pair of staging and private buffers, which means no one else needs to track that pairing (see other comments about how the existing returned pair of Writer and BindInfo should be sufficient from a DrawPass and DrawWriter point of view). But since DBM has the pairs remembered in a  list, we can easily run through them and add copy tasks to the recording (and maybe this means we return a new Task instead of being a void function).",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 182,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 182,
        "endChar": 67
      },
      "revId": "1ecc526bce26299c2cb4e8e7bc298b0030796596",
