      "lineNbr": 152,
      "author": {
        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-11-21T18:29:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think we should add fStagingBuffer to BindBufferInfo. DrawBufferManager already returns a Writer and a BindBufferInfo. Right now the Writer and the BindInfo point to the same data, but when staging buffers are involved I think it should be sufficient that the DrawBufferManager returns a Writer that points into the mapped void* of the staging buffer, but the BindBufferInfo has a `const Buffer*` that refers to the GPU-private buffer that is the target of the buffer-to-buffer copy.\n\nWhen DrawPass is recording commands, it only needs to record the GPU-private buffer for bindings, since that\u0027s holding the actual data. And if it is writing data dynamically to the VertexWriter it can continue to use that directly w/o even realizing that it\u0027s a separate buffer object under the hood.\n\nWe just need to track the staging buffer/private buffer pairs in a different place from DrawCommands::List. My initial thinking when starting this review had been that this would be tracked by DrawPass, but now I\u0027m thinking it should just be DrawBufferManager that can handle it entirely.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 152,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 152,
        "endChar": 43
      },
      "revId": "1ecc526bce26299c2cb4e8e7bc298b0030796596",
